# KiCad design files must never be auto-merged.
#
# A .kicad_pcb or .kicad_sch is a serialized object graph -- UUIDs,
# cross-references and order-sensitive structure that merely happen to be
# stored as text. Git's three-way merge will produce a file that usually
# still parses, carrying duplicate UUIDs, orphaned references and silently
# detached nets rather than an honest error.
#
# `-merge` makes git refuse to invent a result: on conflict it leaves our
# version in the worktree and marks the path conflicted, with no markers
# written into the file. Resolve by taking one side whole
# (git checkout --ours/--theirs) and redoing the other side's work in KiCad.
#
# See docs/GIT.md §2. Diffs stay enabled -- they are unreadable as prose but
# useful for counting what changed.

*.kicad_pcb     -merge
*.kicad_sch     -merge
*.kicad_sym     -merge
*.kicad_mod     -merge
*.kicad_pro     -merge

# Library tables are line-oriented and do merge sanely, so they are
# deliberately absent from the list above.

# 3D models: text formats, but large and never usefully diffed.
*.wrl           -merge -diff
*.step          -merge -diff
*.stp           -merge -diff

# Generated exports, checked in for the case designer.
*.svg           -merge
*.dxf           -merge
